Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||06-29-2001||04:09 PM||||I was just sent some good working motors and I just got everything apart with the old motor out and ready for the new motor. But that long arm that connects the motor with the headlight is not on the new motors and I can't seem to get the old one off to stick it on the new one. <BR>Am I suppose to pry the old arm off and stick it on the new motor or was it suppose to be shipped with the new motors? ||||reg||9
Z||000001||DecadenceR||06-29-2001||04:17 PM||||I just did this 2 days ago.<P>There shoud be a little C shaped clip on the arm, right by where it connects to the motor. Just pop that off, and then you install the new motor, just slide that bar into the hole it came out of and pop the c-clip back on.<BR>It;s pretty easy once the assembly is out. Just 3 bolts and a c-clip on the motor.||||reg||1
